From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aria2_build contributors <aria2-build@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] http: ignore trailing semicolons in Content-Disposition

Many widely deployed CDNs and servers (AWS S3/CloudFront, HuggingFace,
nginx) emit a trailing ';' at the end of Content-Disposition headers.
Trim trailing ';' characters before parsing while using the half-open
range [p, eop) safely (fixing the off-by-one *eop dereference in PR #2153).

Reference: https://github.com/aria2/aria2/issues/1118
Reference: https://github.com/aria2/aria2/pull/2153
---
 src/util.cc | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/util.cc b/src/util.cc
--- a/src/util.cc
+++ b/src/util.cc
@@ -1245,6 +1245,14 @@ ssize_t parse_content_disposition(char* dest, size_t destlen,
   *charsetp = nullptr;
   *charsetlenp = 0;
 
+  // Ignore trailing ';' in Content-Disposition (e.g. CloudFront/S3, nginx).
+  // eop is one-past-the-end for [p, eop), so inspect *(eop - 1).
+  while (p != eop && *(eop - 1) == ';') {
+    A2_LOG_INFO("Non-compliant Content-Disposition header (trailing ';') - "
+                "will ignore it");
+    --eop;
+  }
+
   for (; p != eop; ++p) {
     switch (state) {
     case CD_BEFORE_DISPOSITION_TYPE:
-- 
2.52.0
